 ### SCENARIO-PHASE4-066: Completion-Targeting Live Probe Reports Official Score Or Blocks Honestly
 **Description:** Running Exp 4250 either writes `blocked_arc_live_unreachable` when the SDK import or ARC endpoint reachability precondition fails, writes `complete: margin_triggered_override_kept_exploring_<game>` when the margin-triggered override refuses to commit the induced policy, or writes a terminal-prefixed live artifact after the adapter fixture passes, the anonymous-key SDK enumerates the target environment, the high-margin decision commits the induced policy, the solver executes under a bounded completion-sized action budget, and an open scorecard is read without leaderboard submission. A valid reachable artifact MUST set `solver_completes_level` to the bare boolean `live_env_metrics.levels_completed >= 1`, set `no_leaderboard_submission=true`, set `leaderboard_submission_attempted=false`, set `scorecard_closed=false`, include `live_env_metrics` with `score`, `levels_completed`, `actions_taken`, `baseline_actions`, and `action_budget`, preserve observed-frame level evidence separately from official `EnvironmentScore` evidence, compare against the same LP85 random/greedy floor inside `solver_beats_floor`, set `solver_beats_floor.accuracy.beats=true` only when the scorecard score or levels beat the floor, include `margin_triggered_override` with the pre-registered threshold decision and cited 2606.04323/AggLM sources, and preserve an honest terminal `complete:` verdict when the solver completes zero levels on the live scorecard.
+
+### REQ-PHASE4-067: ARC-AGI-3 Incremental Progress Exp4261 Offline Headroom Attempt
+**Description:** The system SHALL run Exp 4261 as the next offline ARC-AGI-3 monotonic solved-level attempt after Exp 4249 established the `.393` best artifact at 19 cumulative real-env-confirmed levels. It MUST first confirm that `python/carnot/agentic/arc_agi3_world_model.py` imports and that `results/arc3_win_condition_survey.json` plus local fixture metadata load; otherwise it MUST stop with `honest_verdict="blocked_arc_fixtures_missing"`. It MUST not touch `results/trm_runs/`, MUST not train TRM, and MUST keep the conductor stood down. It MUST select exactly one game/level with local headroom beyond the Exp 4249 best, preferring `sc25-635fd71a` L6 when the sixth local baseline exists before falling back to the surveyed `r11l-495a7899` frontier. The offline solver MUST use CPU/cached fixtures, explore-induce-verify evidence, and margin-triggered verifier routing before claiming any level increment. The terminal artifact `results/experiment_4261_arc_incremental_progress.json` MUST include bare top-level fields `honest_verdict`, `total_levels`, `levels_completed`, `game_advanced`, `random_seed`, `reproducibility_checksum`, and `model_specs`, and MUST annotate their principles exactly as follows: `Terminal-prefixed. A +1 advance is success; an honest no-advance (no solvable headroom this window) is COMPLETE and informs the next game pick.`, `BARE int: cumulative solved levels -- must be >=20 (monotonic +1 over the .393 19); the north-star accuracy progress metric.`, `BARE int: NEW real-env-confirmed levels this task -- the falsifiable +1 (>=1), from the solver output not a self-report.`, `The game id advanced -- keeps progress attributable per-game (incremental-progress discipline).`, `Determinism precondition for the solver run.`, `Hash of the solver inputs + trajectory; lets a third party re-run.`, and `The offline solver + verifier routing config; required methodology.`.
+
+### SCENARIO-PHASE4-067: Exp4261 Either Banks One New Level Or Stops With Decision-Grade No-Advance
+**Description:** Running Exp 4261 either writes `blocked_arc_fixtures_missing` when the offline solver import, survey, prior Exp 4249 evidence, or local fixture metadata cannot support the attempt, writes `complete: incremental_progress_no_advance_<game>_L<n>_<reason>` when the selected frontier has no verifier-validated real-env level increment in this bounded window, or writes `success: incremental_progress_<game>_advanced_to_L<n>_total20` only when the offline real environment confirms one new level after the margin-triggered verifier accepts the route. A successful run MUST set `total_levels=20`, `levels_completed=1`, `game_advanced` to the advanced game id, `real_env_confirmed=true`, `verifier_validated=true`, preserve model specs for the offline world-model solver and margin-triggered routing, and compute `reproducibility_checksum` from deterministic solver inputs and trajectory evidence. An honest no-advance run MUST keep `total_levels=19`, set `levels_completed=0`, set `game_advanced="none"`, set `real_env_confirmed=false`, keep the selected `target_game` and `target_level` attributable, and still satisfy the acceptance gate when `honest_verdict` is terminal-prefixed with `complete:`. A blocked run MUST keep `total_levels=19`, set `levels_completed=0`, set `game_advanced="none"`, and still satisfy the acceptance gate because the verdict is terminal-prefixed with `blocked_`.
